WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.320
So for the twelfth day of Christmas we thought we'd have an unboxing.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:21.560
So, the video's not about the cardboard, though the chemistry of cardboard is quite interesting,

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.200
but let's see what's inside.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:33.140
We have another present from our fan, Negayesu Nawa, in Japan.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.880
It's the fourth version of his periodic table clock

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:45.180
and you can see it has a really beautiful spiral going round and round

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:51.420
with all the elements including flerovium [and] livermorium. Really up to date.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:58.200
It's a periodic table clock which will join all the other periodic table clocks in my office

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.480
Brady: How many have you got in there?

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:00.840
I've already got four.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:07.660
Here what we have is a really nice demonstration of the periodic table

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:18.760
and we also have something that summarizes one person's passion for the periodic table.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:26.460
Our fan's passion, and it's a passion that all of us making PeriodicVideos and those that are watching it share.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.560
Chemistry is a fantastic subject.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:38.000
It's really exciting. Even the most boring things like a burnt piece of wood has chemical secrets inside it

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:43.360
So, for day 12 we have Periodic Table Clock

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.940
Sofia's Sodium Tile

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.300
Osmium and Thorium

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.300
Periodic Table Handkerchief

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.200
Charred Beam from our New Lab

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:53.560
A Fan from a Fan

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.180
Anthracite from Pennsylvania

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.020
Guitar Plectrum that glows

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.720
Four Drinking Vessels

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.560
Three Chemical Badges

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.280
Two Periodic Table Bed Covers

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.600
and One Piece of Tartaric Acid from a Swiss Wine Barrel

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.520
Thank you for watching our 12 days of Christmas

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.860
Thank you to everyone who sent us these presents

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:23.820
Thank you to everybody who sent us e-mails, sent us pictures, sent us comments

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:29.080
We're looking forward to sharing lots of Chemistry with you in 2016.

